{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | sed -n '300,760p'\"","aggregated_output":"   300\t   retained `:datom` -- the value a retry appends, without which the\n   301\t   wait is not re-establishable. A put names a stream, never a\n   302\t   cursor cell.\"\n   303\t  [serve! resources entry]\n   304\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))]\n   305\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   306\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :put,\n   307\t                 :yin.k/stream marker,\n   308\t                 :yin.k/value (:datom entry)}}\n   309\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\n   310\t\n   311\t\n   312\t(defn- call-out-cell\n   313\t  \"The emitter's call-out cursor cell -- the response route the\n   314\t   retained call had on the emitter: the cursor entry under\n   315\t   `vm/call-out-cursor-key`, reading the call-out stream under\n   316\t   `vm/call-out-stream-key` at its kept position. nil when the\n   317\t   composition holds no call pair, which no real retained request\n   318\t   does -- the pair is checked before the call parked.\"\n   319\t  [resources]\n   320\t  (let [cursor (get resources vm/call-out-cursor-key)\n   321\t        handle (get resources vm/call-out-stream-key)]\n   322\t    (when (and (map? cursor) (contains? cursor :stream-id) handle)\n   323\t      {:id vm/call-out-cursor-key,\n   324\t       :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key,\n   325\t       :cursor (:cursor cursor)})))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn- lift-retained-request\n   329\t  \"S7.4.3's retained call: a `:put` entry carrying `:request-sent`,\n   330\t   the request the engine holds unsent. Both endpoints are served --\n   331\t   the request stream's marker and the response stream's marker,\n   332\t   `call-out-cell`'s -- and the retained envelope is read out\n   333\t   verbatim (`:request-op`, `:request-args`) beside the kept\n   334\t   response cell (`:yin.k/response-cell`), so a resumer can\n   335\t   re-establish the carried pair: retry through the request\n   336\t   reflection, wait for the response through the response reflection\n   337\t   at the kept position. Either endpoint unservable refuses as\n   338\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that endpoint's identity, before any\n   339\t   value is minted.\"\n   340\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   341\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))\n   342\t        envelope (:datom entry)\n   343\t        route (call-out-cell resources)\n   344\t        resp-h (and route (get resources (:stream-id route)))]\n   345\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   346\t      (if-let [resp-marker (and resp-h (lift-marker serve! resp-h))]\n   347\t        (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id route) resp-h (:cursor route))]\n   348\t          {:pending {:yin.k/reason :ffi-request,\n   349\t                     :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\n   350\t                     :yin.k/request-op (or (apply2/request-op envelope)\n   351\t                                           (:op entry)),\n   352\t                     :yin.k/request-args (apply2/request-args envelope),\n   353\t                     :yin.k/request marker,\n   354\t                     :yin.k/response resp-marker,\n   355\t                     :yin.k/response-cell cid},\n   356\t           :cell? true}\n   357\t          (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))\n   358\t        (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))\n   359\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\n   360\t\n   361\t\n   362\t(defn- lift-link\n   363\t  \"S7.4.3's link variants: the link pair name the engine's own fixed\n   364\t   link keys on a real entry (`module/link-request-resource` and\n   365\t   `module/link-response-resource`), resolved into `:resources`, and\n   366\t   the kept `:cursor` on the response stream\n   367\t   (`module/require-handler` mints it before the envelope is appended)\n   368\t   is the response cell -- a cell like any other, at its kept\n   369\t   position. Both pair markers travel, the engine's `:link-response`\n   370\t   entry retaining its `:request` beside the response side; the\n   371\t   envelope rides verbatim on the request-in-hand variant.\"\n   372\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   373\t  (let [reason (:reason entry)\n   374\t        resp-h (get resources (:response entry))\n   375\t        req-h (get resources (:request entry))\n   376\t        kept (:cursor entry)]\n   377\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec [(:response entry) kept] resp-h kept)]\n   378\t      (let [resp (lift-marker serve! resp-h)\n   379\t            req (lift-marker serve! req-h)]\n   380\t        (if (and resp req)\n   381\t          {:pending (cond-> {:yin.k/reason reason,\n   382\t                             :yin.k/link-id (:link-id entry),\n   383\t                             :yin.k/name (:name entry),\n   384\t                             :yin.k/request req,\n   385\t                             :yin.k/response resp,\n   386\t                             :yin.k/cell cid}\n   387\t                      (= :link-request reason)\n   388\t                      (assoc :yin.k/envelope (:envelope entry))),\n   389\t           :cell? true}\n   390\t          (unsatisfied (local-identity (or req-h resp-h)))))\n   391\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))))\n   392\t\n   393\t\n   394\t(defn- lift-one\n   395\t  \"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into `{:pending data,\n   396\t   :cell? bool}` -- `:cell?` true when the variant names a cursor\n   397\t   cell, which is what puts `:dao.stream.remote/v1` in\n   398\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` -- or an outcome carrying\n   399\t   `:yin.k/status`: `:yin.k/unsatisfied` when a stream cannot be\n   400\t   served or a kept cursor does not survive the codec round trip;\n   401\t   `:yin.k/undecodable`, naming the reason, when the entry is no\n   402\t   variant at all.\"\n   403\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   404\t  (case (:reason entry)\n   405\t    :next\n   406\t    (if (:call-id entry)\n   407\t      (lift-response-wait resources mint codec entry)\n   408\t      (lift-read resources mint codec entry))\n   409\t\n   410\t    :put\n   411\t    (if (:request-sent entry)\n   412\t      (lift-retained-request serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   413\t      (lift-write serve! resources entry))\n   414\t\n   415\t    :link-request (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   416\t\n   417\t    :link-response (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   418\t\n   419\t    :install\n   420\t    {:pending {:yin.k/reason :install, :yin.k/name (:name entry)}}\n   421\t\n   422\t    {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable, :yin.k/reason (:reason entry)}))\n   423\t\n   424\t\n   425\t;; =============================================================================\n   426\t;; Lift: the frame and the single entry\n   427\t;; =============================================================================\n   428\t\n   429\t(defn lift-frame\n   430\t  \"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pending entries, lifted together:\n   431\t   `{:yin.k/pending [data ...], :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\n   432\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success -- the cells minted across\n   433\t   the WHOLE set, so two waiters on one engine cursor cell lift to\n   434\t   one UCF cell (S7.5.3) and `:dao.stream.remote/v1` rides in\n   435\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` when any entry names a cell; the S7.9\n   436\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` outcome, naming the stream identity where one\n   437\t   is known, when any entry's stream cannot be served or its kept\n   438\t   cursor does not survive the codec round trip; the S7.9\n   439\t   `:yin.k/undecodable` outcome when any entry names no variant.\n   440\t   Failure is total (S7.5.4): a refused leaf refuses the frame.\"\n   441\t  ([serve! resources entries]\n   442\t   (lift-frame serve! resources entries cursor-codec))\n   443\t  ([serve! resources entries codec]\n   444\t   (let [found (atom {:cells {}, :of {}})\n   445\t         mint (mint-cell serve! found)\n   446\t         lifted (mapv #(lift-one serve! resources mint codec %) entries)]\n   447\t     (if-let [refusal (some #(when (contains? % :yin.k/status) %) lifted)]\n   448\t       refusal\n   449\t       {:yin.k/pending (mapv :pending lifted),\n   450\t        :yin.k/cells (:cells @found),\n   451\t        :yin.k/requires (if (some :cell? lifted) requires {})}))))\n   452\t\n   453\t\n   454\t(defn lift-pending\n   455\t  \"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into its own self-contained\n   456\t   cell table: `{:yin.k/pending data, :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\n   457\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success, with the same `:yin.k/\n   458\t   unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes `lift-frame`\n   459\t   gives. Frame assembly that shares cells across entries is\n   460\t   `lift-frame`'s.\"\n   461\t  ([serve! resources entry]\n   462\t   (lift-pending serve! resources entry cursor-codec))\n   463\t  ([serve! resources entry codec]\n   464\t   (let [r (lift-frame serve! resources [entry] codec)]\n   465\t     (if (contains? r :yin.k/status)\n   466\t       r\n   467\t       (assoc r :yin.k/pending (first (:yin.k/pending r)))))))\n   468\t\n   469\t\n   470\t;; =============================================================================\n   471\t;; Lower: back into resources and a wait-set entry\n   472\t;; =============================================================================\n   473\t\n   474\t(def ^:private fixed-resource-keys\n   475\t  \"The VM's fixed private resource keys -- the FFI call pair and the\n   476\t   link pair. Batch-allocated keys never collide with them, and the\n   477\t   lower installs nothing at them but what the engine's own dispatch\n   478\t   reads there: the link pair, and a retained request's fixed local\n   479\t   call-in key.\"\n   480\t  #{vm/call-in-stream-key vm/call-out-stream-key\n   481\t    vm/call-out-cursor-key module/link-request-resource\n   482\t    module/link-response-resource})\n   483\t\n   484\t\n   485\t(defn- fresh-key\n   486\t  \"The next private resource key `used` does not hold, claiming it:\n   487\t   `:yin.k/k-1`, `:yin.k/k-2`, ... regenerating on any collision\n   488\t   with the receiver's existing resources, the VM's fixed keys, or\n   489\t   keys this batch already allocated.\"\n   490\t  [used]\n   491\t  (loop [n (inc (count @used))]\n   492\t    (let [k (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"k-\" n))]\n   493\t      (if (contains? @used k)\n   494\t        (recur (inc n))\n   495\t        (do (swap! used conj k) k)))))\n   496\t\n   497\t\n   498\t(defn- pending-markers\n   499\t  \"Every stream marker `pending` names beside its cells' -- the\n   500\t   target of a put, both endpoints of a retained call, the pair of\n   501\t   a link request.\"\n   502\t  [pending]\n   503\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   504\t    :put [(:yin.k/stream pending)]\n   505\t    :ffi-request [(:yin.k/request pending)\n   506\t                  (:yin.k/response pending)]\n   507\t    (:link-request :link-response)\n   508\t    [(:yin.k/request pending)\n   509\t     (:yin.k/response pending)]\n   510\t    []))\n   511\t\n   512\t\n   513\t(defn- attach-all\n   514\t  \"One attach per distinct stream identity. The first attach that\n   515\t   does not answer ok -- a reflection marked gone included -- refuses\n   516\t   the lower as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that identity. Returns\n   517\t   {:handles {identity handle}}; `lower-frame` allocates each\n   518\t   reflection its own collision-free resource key.\"\n   519\t  [attach! markers]\n   520\t  (let [by-id (reduce (fn [m mkr]\n   521\t                        (update m (:dao.stream/identity mkr) #(or % mkr)))\n   522\t                      {} markers)]\n   523\t    (reduce-kv (fn [acc identity mkr]\n   524\t                 (if-let [h (lower-marker attach! mkr)]\n   525\t                   (assoc-in acc [:handles identity] h)\n   526\t                   (reduced (unsatisfied identity))))\n   527\t               {:handles {}}\n   528\t               by-id)))\n   529\t\n   530\t\n   531\t(defn- cell-resources\n   532\t  \"The fresh cursor entry each UCF cell lowers to, under the key\n   533\t   `cell-keys` allocated for it: its carried position, on the\n   534\t   reflection of the stream the cell names. Two references to one\n   535\t   cell share the one entry, and one ref per cell keeps its own\n   536\t   (S7.5.3); equal cell ids across separately lowered frames got\n   537\t   different keys, so no two frames ever share an entry. A response\n   538\t   route is no exception: it lowers under its own fresh key, never\n   539\t   at a fixed key, so distinct routes stay distinct and no migrated\n   540\t   route can ever misroute a new call.\"\n   541\t  [streams cells cell-keys]\n   542\t  (into {}\n   543\t        (map (fn [[cid cell]]\n   544\t               [(cell-keys cid)\n   545\t                {:stream-id (streams (cell-identity cells cid)),\n   546\t                 :cursor (:yin.k/position cell)}]))\n   547\t        cells))\n   548\t\n   549\t\n   550\t(defn- link-pair-resources\n   551\t  \"The engine's fixed link keys (`module/link-request-resource`,\n   552\t   `module/link-response-resource`) mapped onto the reflections a\n   553\t   lowered link wait uses: the engine's sweep retries a\n   554\t   `:link-request` by appending at the fixed request key\n   555\t   (`module/append-link-request`) and polls a `:link-response` at the\n   556\t   fixed response key (`poll-link-response`), so a lowered link wait\n   557\t   parks where the engine looks. One pair per task: the identity of\n   558\t   each side rides the pending's own markers.\"\n   559\t  [streams resources pendings]\n   560\t  (reduce (fn [acc pending]\n   561\t            (if (contains? #{:link-request :link-response}\n   562\t                           (:yin.k/reason pending))\n   563\t              (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   564\t                                            :dao.stream/identity])\n   565\t                    resp-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/response\n   566\t                                             :dao.stream/identity])\n   567\t                    req (get resources (streams req-id))\n   568\t                    resp (get resources (streams resp-id))]\n   569\t                (if (and req resp)\n   570\t                  (assoc acc\n   571\t                         module/link-request-resource req,\n   572\t                         module/link-response-resource resp)\n   573\t                  acc))\n   574\t              acc))\n   575\t          {}\n   576\t          pendings))\n   577\t\n   578\t\n   579\t(defn- lower-one\n   580\t  \"One pending of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e}` -- the wait-set\n   581\t   entry the receiver parks, the caller's register context `ctx`\n   582\t   merged verbatim under the stream and cell fields the data\n   583\t   rebuilds -- or an outcome carrying `:yin.k/status`, naming the\n   584\t   stream identity where one is known. Every wait polls the key\n   585\t   `cell-keys` allocated for its cell, reading the stream key\n   586\t   `streams` allocated for the cell's reflection: migrated waits\n   587\t   poll routes no new call shares. A retained request's retry\n   588\t   writes through the request reflection's allocated key and stamps\n   589\t   the carried response route (`:response-cursor`,\n   590\t   `:response-stream`) for its restore.\"\n   591\t  [pending ctx streams cells cell-keys]\n   592\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   593\t    :next\n   594\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\n   595\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\n   596\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   597\t                       {:reason :next,\n   598\t                        :stream-id sid,\n   599\t                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref,\n   600\t                                     :id (cell-keys cid)}})}\n   601\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   602\t\n   603\t    :put\n   604\t    (if-let [sid (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream\n   605\t                                           :dao.stream/identity]))]\n   606\t      {:entry (merge ctx\n   607\t                     {:reason :put,\n   608\t                      :stream-id sid,\n   609\t                      :datom (:yin.k/value pending)})}\n   610\t      (unsatisfied (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream :dao.stream/identity])))\n   611\t\n   612\t    :ffi\n   613\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\n   614\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\n   615\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   616\t                       (cond-> {:reason :next,\n   617\t                                :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\n   618\t                                :stream-id sid,\n   619\t                                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref,\n   620\t                                             :id (cell-keys cid)}}\n   621\t                         (contains? pending :yin.k/op)\n   622\t                         (assoc :op (:yin.k/op pending))))}\n   623\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   624\t\n   625\t    :ffi-request\n   626\t    (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   627\t                                  :dao.stream/identity])\n   628\t          resp-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/response\n   629\t                                   :dao.stream/identity])]\n   630\t      (if-let [req (streams req-id)]\n   631\t        (if-let [resp (streams resp-id)]\n   632\t          {:entry (merge ctx\n   633\t                         {:reason :put,\n   634\t                          :request-sent true,\n   635\t                          :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\n   636\t                          :op (:yin.k/request-op pending),\n   637\t                          :stream-id req,\n   638\t                          :datom (apply2/request\n   639\t                                   (:yin.k/call-id pending)\n   640\t                                   (:yin.k/request-op pending)\n   641\t                                   (:yin.k/request-args pending)),\n   642\t                          :response-cursor\n   643\t                          (cell-keys (:yin.k/response-cell pending)),\n   644\t                          :response-stream resp})}\n   645\t          (unsatisfied resp-id))\n   646\t        (unsatisfied req-id)))\n   647\t\n   648\t    (:link-request :link-response)\n   649\t    (let [reason (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   650\t          cid (:yin.k/cell pending)\n   651\t          sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))\n   652\t          req (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   653\t                                        :dao.stream/identity]))]\n   654\t      (if (and sid req)\n   655\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   656\t                       (cond-> {:reason reason,\n   657\t                                :link-id (:yin.k/link-id pending),\n   658\t                                :name (:yin.k/name pending),\n   659\t                                :request module/link-request-resource,\n   660\t                                :response module/link-response-resource,\n   661\t                                :cursor (:yin.k/position (get cells cid))}\n   662\t                         (= :link-request reason)\n   663\t                         (assoc :envelope (:yin.k/envelope pending))))}\n   664\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   665\t\n   666\t    :install\n   667\t    {:entry (merge ctx\n   668\t                   {:reason :install, :name (:yin.k/name pending)})}\n   669\t\n   670\t    {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable,\n   671\t     :yin.k/reason (:yin.k/reason pending)}))\n   672\t\n   673\t\n   674\t(defn lower-frame\n   675\t  \"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pendings, lowered together as one\n   676\t   batch: `{:entries [e ...], :resources table}` -- one private\n   677\t   resource key allocated per distinct served identity and one per\n   678\t   distinct UCF cell, two waiters on one cell lowering back into one\n   679\t   shared entry and independent cells staying independent (S7.5.3);\n   680\t   equal cell ids across separately lowered frames get different\n   681\t   keys. `occupied` is the receiver's existing resource keys: every\n   682\t   allocated key is checked against it, against the VM's fixed\n   683\t   resource keys, and against keys already allocated in the batch,\n   684\t   regenerating on collision. With the same `:yin.k/unsatisfied` and\n   685\t   `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes `lift-frame` gives. Where the engine\n   686\t   resolves a wait at one of its own fixed resource keys, the lower\n   687\t   parks the wait there: a link wait's pair under\n   688\t   `module/link-request-resource` and `module/link-response-resource`.\n   689\t   A retained request's retry writes through its carried request\n   690\t   reflection's allocated key and stamps the carried response route\n   691\t   (`:response-cursor`, `:response-stream`) for its restore.\n   692\t   `contexts`, parallel to `pendings`, is each entry's register\n   693\t   context, merged verbatim.\"\n   694\t  ([attach! pendings cells contexts]\n   695\t   (lower-frame attach! pendings cells contexts nil))\n   696\t  ([attach! pendings cells contexts occupied]\n   697\t   (let [ms (distinct (remove nil?\n   698\t                              (concat (map :yin.k/stream (vals cells))\n   699\t                                      (mapcat pending-markers pendings))))\n   700\t         a (attach-all attach! ms)]\n   701\t     (if (contains? a :yin.k/status)\n   702\t       a\n   703\t       (let [used (atom (into fixed-resource-keys occupied))\n   704\t             handles (:handles a)\n   705\t             streams (into {}\n   706\t                           (map (fn [identity]\n   707\t                                  [identity (fresh-key used)]))\n   708\t                           (sort-by str (keys handles)))\n   709\t             resources (into {}\n   710\t                             (map (fn [[identity sid]]\n   711\t                                    [sid (handles identity)]))\n   712\t                             streams)\n   713\t             cell-keys (into {}\n   714\t                             (map (fn [cid] [cid (fresh-key used)]))\n   715\t                             (sort-by str (keys cells)))\n   716\t             lowered (mapv #(lower-one %1 %2 streams cells cell-keys)\n   717\t                           pendings contexts)]\n   718\t         (if-let [refusal (some #(when (contains? % :yin.k/status) %)\n   719\t                                lowered)]\n   720\t           refusal\n   721\t           {:entries (mapv :entry lowered),\n   722\t            :resources (merge resources\n   723\t                              (cell-resources streams cells cell-keys)\n   724\t                              (link-pair-resources streams resources\n   725\t                                                   pendings))}))))))\n   726\t\n   727\t\n   728\t(defn lower-pending\n   729\t  \"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e, :resources\n   730\t   table}` -- the wait-set entry `ctx`'s registers ride on, and the\n   731\t   fresh resource entries it polls through -- with the same\n   732\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes\n   733\t   `lower-frame` gives. `occupied` is the receiver's existing\n   734\t   resource keys, as `lower-frame`'s. Frame assembly that shares\n   735\t   cursor entries across entries is `lower-frame`'s.\"\n   736\t  ([attach! pending cells ctx]\n   737\t   (lower-pending attach! pending cells ctx nil))\n   738\t  ([attach! pending cells ctx occupied]\n   739\t   (let [r (lower-frame attach! [pending] cells [ctx] occupied)]\n   740\t     (if (contains? r :yin.k/status)\n   741\t       r\n   742\t       (-> r\n   743\t           (assoc :entry (first (:entries r)))\n   744\t           (dissoc :entries))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
